5
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:43,000
Then Bee's own alarm arrives as a notification. No custom app: it is all native Bee.

6
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Here is the Bee app on my iPhone, capturing live.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:53,000
And the to-dos Nectar created are right there in Bee's own app, each with its alarm.

8
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
It is built entirely on Bee's own interfaces, all in one folder.

9
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
The Bee proxy's REST API for to-dos, facts, conversations and the changefeed.

10
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,500
And the Bee CLI for the live stream, today's brief and the MCP server.

11
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:14,500
The model is real too: Claude Haiku through Anthropic's API, as the console shows.

12
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:20,500
It is open source on GitHub, with a README that explains how it uses Bee.

13
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:23,500
No custom watch app, only native Bee.

14
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,500
CI is green on every push.

15
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:30,500
